   "title": "Real In, Real Out: What If We Only Use Real Data for Scene Text Editing?",
   "snippet": "Aiming to modify textual content while preserving the original style, Scene Text Editing (STE) has significant practical value in many applications. STE typically requires paired images before and after editing for training. However, recent approaches rely heavily on synthetic paired data and complex disentanglement strategies. They struggle to faithfully capture the diversity and complexity of na",
